<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Regional Index Fund raises S$249 mln.</title>
<headline>Singapore Regional Index Fund raises S$249 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Consortium Investment Management Ltd said the Singapore Regional Index Fund had raised a record Singapore $249 million by the end of Wednesday's launch date.</p>
<p>The consortium -- comprising DBS Bank, Keppel Bank, OCBC Bank, OUB, Tat Lee Bank and UOB Bank -- said in a statement S$182 million was from retail investors. This represents the largest amount raised by any unit trust in Singapore.</p>
<p>The Fund will start trading on the Stock Exchange of Singapore on a &quot;when issued&quot; basis on December 20.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
